// Payment intent API (RFC 0001 §1.5, §2.2.5, §4.4.5). The realtime gateway
// calls it for the THROW, CATCH and delivery receipts of the people it
// authenticated (access token and DPoP proof in HELLO) and names them in
// `actor`; only workloads trusted under the mTLS ACL may call it. The
// gateway's REST API serves the same operations to apps directly.
//
// Conventions:
//   - Ids are canonical UUID strings; amounts are int64 minor units.
//   - CreateIntent is idempotent per intent id: the same TxAuth bytes return
//     the intent (and finish any pending ledger step). Catch, Cancel and
//     MarkDelivered are idempotent too.
//   - Failures carry a google.rpc.ErrorInfo with domain "intents.bilyon" and
//     a reason (TXAUTH, NONCE, STALE, MISMATCH, CONFLICT, NOT_FOUND,
//     FORBIDDEN, STATE, INVALID, UNAVAILABLE). STATE errors carry the
//     intent's state in metadata["state"].

